  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "Tai Bai Yun Sheng’s Tai Bai blessed land has the least earth path dao marks, so it has no mountains and the soil is infertile.",
      "chapters": [
        821
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_tai_bai_yun_sheng",
        "loc_tai_bai_blessed_land"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "After Hu Immortal blessed land’s swamp crab earthly calamity, small amounts of earth path dao marks were added: they increase soil fertility, make the ground firmer, help the land absorb earth qi, and support Dang Hun Mountain. Earlier tribulations for Hu Immortal likewise added wood path and earth path dao marks that remodeled the blessed land’s environment so stronger plants could grow.",
      "chapters": [
        826
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "loc_hu_immortal_blessed_land",
        "loc_dang_hun_mountain",
        "char_fairy_bai_hu"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "General dao marks and attainment levels are covered on dao marks and attainment.",
      "chapters": [],
      "certainty": "inferred",
      "confidence": "C",
      "verification": "no_citation",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_dao_marks"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Rockmen are born with earth path dao marks. Shi Nu’s earth path cultivation is especially useful in an environment like Earth Abyss.",
      "chapters": [
        1067
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "rockmen-from-birth",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "race_rockmen",
        "char_shi_nu",
        "reg_earth_earth_abyss"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Fang Yuan’s sovereign immortal aperture has few earth path dao marks spread across a vast space. With few earth path dao marks, mountains do not form and the soil is neither thick nor fertile, so vegetation transplanted from Hei Fan grotto-heaven dries out. Mortal fertile soils only hold fragmented earth path dao marks that dissipate after plants absorb their nutrients. The lasting fix is to raise earth path dao marks in the aperture through tribulation or by absorbing an earth path Gu Immortal’s marks.",
      "chapters": [
        1148
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "sparse-aperture-soil",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_fang_yuan",
        "loc_hei_fan_grotto_heaven",
        "sys_gu_immortal"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Southern Border has the most earth path dao marks of the five regions, and its earth vein is the deepest among them, so earth vein tremors hit it first when the great era arrives.",
      "chapters": [
        1408
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "southern-border-density",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "reg_southern_border"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Flying Sand Pavilion can use earth path dao marks to cut immortal essence expenditure and raise speed; in Southern Border’s mountains and forests those marks are extremely dense, so the Immortal Gu House moves like a fish in water.",
      "chapters": [
        1386
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "southern-border-density",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "house_flying_sand_pavilion",
        "sys_immortal_gu_house"
      ]
    }
